<title>BELGIUM: Bernheim-Comofi makes French acquisition.</title>
<headline>Bernheim-Comofi makes French acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian property company Bernheim-Comofi said on Saturday its  Interparking car park business had expanded in France by taking control of  Codeparc SA, a unit of Cie de Suez.</p>
<p>&quot;The Interparking Group has bought from Suez the whole of its public car parks business which was held by Codeparc and subsidiaries,&quot; Bernheim-Comofi said in a notice published in Belgian newspapers.</p>
<p>The acquistion takes Interparking's number of parking spaces in France to around 13,500 from 5,000, and the company's total number of spaces to more than 100,000, Bernheim-Comofi said.</p>
<p>Interparking is Europe's leading car parks operator, and number one in Belgium, it said.</p>
<p>Bernheim-Comofi owns 50 percent of Interparking. The remaining shares are held by family-controlled holding company Parfinco.</p>
